<title>FRANCE: Tietmeyer-Germany still interested in stable mark.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer-Germany still interested in stable mark.</headline>
<dateline>LYON, France 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer, reaffirming that Germany remains interested in a stable mark, said on Tuesday he was not interested in a foreign exchange correction that goes beyond fundamentals.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer told a news conference after a Franco-German summit the statement by finance leaders at the G7 meeting last month in Berlin, which said the dollar's correction has been completed, has been clearly understood by markets.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not want to see a correction that goes beyond the market fundamentals,&quot; Tietmeyer said. &quot;We are interested in a stable mark.&quot;</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
